1 NOTE {geni:about_me} --------------------
2 CONT https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/J%C3%B6ns_Jacob_Berzelius
2 CONT
2 CONT Baron Jöns Jacob Berzelius (Swedish: [jœns ˌjɑːkɔb bæɹˈseːliɵs]; 20 August 1779 – 7 August 1848), named by himself and contemporary society as Jacob Berzelius, was a Swedish chemist. Berzelius is considered, along with Robert Boyl
2 CONC e, John Dalton, and Antoine Lavoisier, to be one of the founders of modern chemistry.
2 CONT
2 CONT Berzelius began his career as a physician but his researches in physical chemistry were of lasting significance in the development of the subject. He is especially noted for his determination of atomic weights; his experiments led
2 CONC  to a more complete depiction of the principles of stoichiometry, or the field of chemical combining proportions. In 1803 Berzelius demonstrated the power of an electrochemical cell to decompose chemicals into pairs of electricall
2 CONC y opposite constituents.
2 CONT
2 CONT Berzelius's work with atomic weights and his theory of electrochemical dualism led to his development of a modern system of chemical formula notation that could portray the composition of any compound both qualitatively (by showin
2 CONC g its electrochemically opposing ingredients) and quantitatively (by showing the proportions in which the ingredients were united). His system abbreviated the Latin names of the elements with one or two letters and applied supersc
2 CONC ripts to designate the number of atoms of each element present in both the acidic and basic ingredients.
2 CONT
2 CONT Berzelius himself discovered and isolated several new elements, including cerium (1803) and thorium (1828). Berzelius’s interest in mineralogy also fostered his analysis and preparation of new compounds of these and other elements
2 CONC . The mineral berzelianite was discovered in 1850 and named after him. He was a strict empiricist and insisted that any new theory be consistent with the sum of chemical knowledge. He developed classical analytical techniques, and
2 CONC  investigated isomerism and catalysis, phenomena that owe their names to him. He became a member of the Royal Swedish Academy of Sciences in 1808 and served from 1818 as its principal functionary, the perpetual secretary. He is kn
2 CONC own in Sweden as "the Father of Swedish Chemistry". Berzelius Day is celebrated on 20 August in honour of him.
2 CONT --------------------
2 CONT === GEDCOM Note ===
2 CONT Kemist. Upptäckte Selen och Kisel
2 CONT
2 CONT === GEDCOM Note ===
2 CONT Jöns Jakob Berzelius föddes i en lärarfamilj i Väversunda kyrkby i Östergötland 20 augusti 1779 som son till Samuel Berzelius och Dorotea Sjösten. Han blev tidigt föräldralös och togs först omhand av en styvfar och senare en morbr
2 CONC or, där han nästan var som en tiggare.
2 CONT
2 CONT https://www.geni.com/people/Clas-Fredric-Hornstedt/6000000115662024855 var här hans lärare och kom att betyda mycket för hans naturvetenskapliga intresse.
2 CONT
2 CONT Biografi https://ki.se/om-ki/jons-jacob-berzelius
2 CONT
