1 NAME Jacob Jacob /Lallerstedt/
2 GIVN Jacob Jacob
2 SURN Lallerstedt
2 _MARNM Letterstedt
1 SEX M
1 BIRT
2 DATE 15 DEC 1796
2 ADDR
3 STAE Östergötland County
3 CTRY Sweden
1 DEAT
2 DATE 18 MAR 1862
2 PLAC Frankrike (I Paris, begr i Vallerstad) 
2 ADDR
1 NOTE {geni:about_me} http://www.nad.riksarkivet.se/sbl/Presentation.aspx?id=11244
2 CONT
2 CONT http://runeberg.org/millionar/8/0182.html
2 CONT
2 CONT Jacob Lettersted word bekend as ’n vooruitstrewende man , met behulp van sy vrou se Dreyer-erfgoed. Letterstedt was ’n gekultiveerde man. Hy word konsul vir Noorwee en Swede in Suid-Afrika. In die Cory Biblioteek in Grahamstad is 
2 CONC daar blykbaar kopiee van die korrespondensie wat hy gevoer het met die vermaarde Sweedse naturalis, versamelaar en ontdekkingsreisiger Johan August Wahlberg (1810-1856) SA Who’s Who Ancestry24. Die opvoedkundige, wiskundige en Ang
2 CONC likaanse priester George Frederick Childe wat sedert 1852 vir meer as 25 jaar professor in wiskunde en natuurlike filosofie was aan die Suid-Afrikaanse Kollege was blykbaar ook ’n vriend van die Letterstedts. Die priester en sy vr
2 CONC ou Catherine Mills vernoem dan ook hulle jonger seun Letterstedt Frederick Childe (1859 – 1915). Laasgenoemde word later hoof van die Grant Medical College in Bombaai.
2 CONT
2 CONT In “Rondebosch down the years 1657-1957” ed F. J. Wagener (1957), in ’n besprekiing van die ou landgoedere in Rondebosch, word die volgende genoem:
2 CONT
2 CONT “Mariendahl, formerly Questenburg and Louwvliet, was the property of the Hon. Jacob Letterstedt for many years after 1845. He established a brewery on his estate but was one of the several who sold out to the all-powerful Anders O
2 CONC hlsson who established his principal factory at Mariendahl in 1900. The Western Province Cricket Club ground was opened in 1888 and the Rugby ground in 1890. The boundaries are most complicated but may be traced by following the L
2 CONC iesbeek, Dulwich Road, the railway, the northern fence of the cricket ground, Palmyra Road, Stegmann Road, Vineyard Road to Corwen Street and thence a line to the top of Sans Souci Road and down that road to the river.
2 CONT
2 CONT Before concluding, mention must be made of the Albion Mill Estate which lies between the Main Road and the Liesbeek from Westerford Bridge to Schweppes’ factory. The Albion Mill was situated where the mineral water factory is now 
2 CONC making valuable use of the clear waters of the famed Albion Spring which rises there.
2 CONT
2 CONT Another water mill, derelict these many years, is in Boundary Road opposite the Brewery. This was Letterstedt’s or Josephine’s Mill, named after Crown Princess Josephine who became Queen Josephine of Sweden in 1844
2 CONT
2 CONT Franken & Cook, in hul bespreking van Josephine Mill (Boundary Rd), korrigeer hierdie laaste bewering: Josephine Mill is vernoem na Kroonprinses Josephine van Swede, Letterstedt se geboorteland. Josephine Mill is in 1840 gebou op 
2 CONC die Mariendahl landgoed
2 CONT
2 CONT As ’n interessante brokkie hierby: in die Grahamstown Journal 6 Jan 1832 verskyn die volgende “domestic announcement”:
2 CONT
2 CONT “JH SMITH begs leave to inform the inhabitants of Grahamstown and vicinity that he has taken out a wholesale spirit licence, and has at present for sale, good old Cape brandy, bottled ale and Porter, and few hogsheads ofLettersted
2 CONC t's superior Pale Ale and will shortly receive foreign wines and spirits which will be sold at reduced prices.”
2 CONT
2 CONT Maria Barendina is in 1848 (MOOC 9525) oorlede. Sy is begrawe in ’n Dreyer/Letterstedt familiegrafkelder in die Wynberg NG Kerk Begraafplaas, waar ’n kleinseun van haar vorige man, Jakob Gustaaf Lettersted Dreyer, ook begrawe is. 
2 CONC Oor hierdie grafkelder skryf Wilma Malherbe as volg op Buiteposten oor ’n uitknipsel in haar besit: “think it was published in an issue of Capensis, but it may be Cabo”:
2 CONT
2 CONT There is for instance, Jakob Gustav Letterstedt Dreyer, owner of Kleine Schuur who founded the congregation of Rondebosch...to the left of the group (of four vault tombs in the centre of the cemetery, arranged in a fan-like fashio
2 CONC n) a mound of rubble overgrown with weeds completed the "fan". Close scrutiny of the building material established that this was in fact the remains of a fifth vault similar in design and dating from the same period.
2 CONT
2 CONT It was known that Marina Barendina Bekker, the wealthy widow Dreyer who subsequently married Jacob (sic) Letterstedt, had been a member of the Wynberg congregation and had been buried in the cemetery after her death in 1848. All t
2 CONC races of her grave had, however, disappeared. Of the many damaged graves and illegible headstones in the cemetery, none seemed worthy of her. Furthermore the date of her death and her position in the community led one to expect he
2 CONC r to be buried in a vault. That the ruined vault in the middle was in fact her last resting place remained mere conjecture until the discovery of an old document at the back of the safe in the Wynberg Church listing the first hund
2 CONC red owners of burial plots in the cemetery. Heading the list are the names of the owners of the five oldest vaults, among them J.Letterstedt.
2 CONT
2 CONT Na die dood van Maria Barendina trou Letterstedt in 1851 vir die tweede keer en wel met ’n Engelse dame Lydia Meredyth Boys (daar is rekord van ’n huwelik 1851 St Martin in the Fields Middlesex Engeland) Later jare het hy na Parys
2 CONC  Frankryk uitgewyk en sterf daar in 1862 (MOOC 9559). Hulle het een dogter Lydia wat later trou met Viscount de Montmort en aan die Kaap woon. Sien “Mills of Southern Africa” vir meer info oor Letterstedt. Ook die bydrae oor Josep
2 CONC hine’s Mill in The Best of the Cape Odessey Vol 1.
2 CONT
2 CONT In 1849 raak Letterstedt betrokke in een van die mees berugte hofsake van sy tyd. Die saak spruit uit ’n besluit van XX om die Kaap as ’n strafkolonie te gebruik en ’n skip vol prisoniers hierheen stuur. Hoewel Lettersted ook teen
2 CONC  hierdie plan vir die Kaap was, het hy geweier om mee te doen aan die boikot van die skip toe die in die Kaap land. Terwyl die boikotters geweier het om dit van voorrade te voorsien. Het Letterstedt dit egter wel gedoen, uit human
2 CONC itere oorwegings – wat hom die intense gramskap van sy medeburgers op die hals gehaal het, in die mate dat hulle sy eiendom beskadig het en hom aangerand het. Letterstedt maak ’n saak van laster aanhangig teen mede-lede van die An
2 CONC ti-Convict Association George Morgan, John Fairbairn, Thomas Sutherland, John van Reenen en Olof Bergh. Sir Christoffel Joseph Brand, advokaat, joernalis en eerste Speaker van die Kaapse parlement tree vir Letterstedt op, maar die
2 CONC  hof het Letterstedt se eis om skadevergoeding nie gunstig aangehoor nie – te midde van hewige argument tussen die drie regters.
2 CONT
2 CONT Die hele episode het hom redelik verbitterd gelaat sodat hy meer en meer tyd in die buiteland begin deurbring het, waar hy dan ook uiteindelik in Parys oorlede is........................----Jean Marais
2 CONT
2 CONT In the 1840s, Jacob Letterstedt, a well-connected businessman with varied interests, set up Mariendahl Brewery and Josephine’s Mill, making use of the natural spring water from Newlands Spring for the brewing of his beer. He also 
2 CONC imported modern, updated equipment and expertise, which resulted in much better quality beer than was previously available. At the same time, there was another substantial brewing operation, Newlands Brewery, which was situated be
2 CONC low the current Forrester’s Arms and brewed much more beer than Mariendahl Brewery.
2 CONT
2 CONT In 1864, Anders Ohlsson came to the Cape and by 1881 had bought up a variety of commercial enterprises, one of which was a mill not far from the breweries. He had assessed that brewing had a bright future and proceeded to purchase
2 CONC  properties in the area. In 1888, Ohlsson ended up leasing the Mariendahl Brewery and Josephine’s Mill with an option to buy all the leased properties and water rights from Newlands Spring. In this time he had also negotiated purc
2 CONC hase of or rights to a number of other breweries in the area, namely the Martienessen Brewery, the substantial Cannon Brewery, and eventually the Newlands Brewery after the death of its owner. (it was only 30 years after Jacob Let
2 CONC terstedt death that Lydia (his daughter) and her husband leased to Ohlsson in 1888 and bought it in 1889.)
